    "detailed_description": "<strong>WARNING:</strong> This game may trigger seizures in people with photosensitive epilepsy. It may cause heart palpitations. It is left to the player's discretion.<br><br>&quot;HOW MUCH PATIENCE MAY REQUIRE TO COMPANY A DEAD BODY?&quot;<br><br><strong>IMPORTANT NOTE:</strong> The game focuses on exploration and slowly builds tension to create a deeper and more meaningful experience. The story of the game can cause a lot of discomfort as it is supported by light, loud and sudden sounds. Take into consideration that it makes you feel a lot of fear and it is a psychologically difficult game.<br>CHAPERONE is a first-person psychological horror game.<br><br><strong>Environment</strong><br>In the game where we start our duty as a police officer, the police house consists of two different houses that we will later investigate.<br><br><strong>About The Game</strong><br>In this game, inspired by real events in 2001, your aim is to solve a murder whose cause is unknown, become a companion for the body found in the house at the time, and reach the truth that disturbs the dead body.<br><br><strong>Supernatural entities</strong><br>Paranormal entities that are constantly unknown where and when they will appear.<br><br><strong>Developer's comment about the game</strong><br>Chaperone can leave an impact on your psychology. We recommend that people who are afraid of the dark, have heart disease, or are afraid of being alone should not play alone.<br><br><strong>IMPORTANT NOTE:</strong><br>Chaperone was inspired by a real event that took place in Munich, Germany in 2001. If research is done, you can still find issues similar to this story today...",
